=begin
  trash-sort.lic

  Clears the cheap things out of your vault. Walks to your hometown's
  Carousel and opens the vault the way ;stash does, then takes each thing out
  of the vault in turn and APPRAISEs it:
    - under 10,000 Kronars: down the vault's garbage chute
    - anything else: back in the vault
  Every value is written down in Lich's data/DR/<character>/trash-sort.yaml,
  and anything thrown out comes off ;stash's list (stash.yaml), so ;unstash
  doesn't look for it.

  It leaves you in the vault chamber with the vault open, because the chute
  holds what's thrown in until you leave the chamber ("A flap prevents it
  from falling all the way down until you leave the chamber"). Check the
  chute for anything you still want, put it back in the vault, then CLOSE
  VAULT and leave.

  What's in the vault comes from RUMMAGE VAULT, which lists all of it. LOOK IN
  VAULT stops partway through a full vault with "a lot of other stuff"
  (2026-11-21: it showed 73 things of more than 150), so it's only used if
  RUMMAGE doesn't answer. If the list ends with "a lot of other stuff", the
  vault is listed again each time something has gone down the chute, which
  lets it show more.

  Never thrown out, and not even picked up:
    - crafting tools and supplies: your yaml's *_tools, what ;stash put in the
      vault as tools, and books, logbooks, instructions, oil, flux and founts
    - your weapons and gear (the yaml's weapon_training and gear)
    - the stock ;unstash marathon gets out for ;taskmaster marathon: burlap
      cloth, rat-pelt leather, wool yarn and cotton thread
    - anything the sorter files as crafting gear, stacker, trainer, container
      or box (base-sorting.yaml), like the vault's large shelf
  Crafting materials aren't tools, so they're appraised like everything else:
  ingots, nuggets, bars, lumps, fragments, shards, deeds, stacks, stones,
  beads, sigil-scrolls, leather, cloth, yarn, thread and dyes (except the four
  marathon stocks; a cleaning, chamois or polishing cloth is a tool).
  And kept after APPRAISE:
    - containers ("The dark gem pouch is a container."), which may hold
      something
    - anything APPRAISE doesn't give an exact Kronar figure for: "worth
      exactly nothing" (memory orbs appraise like that, 2026-11-21), "probably
      worth around several thousand", or a value in another currency
  Something trash-sort.yaml already has as kept at 10K or more isn't
  appraised again.

  Usage:
    ;trash-sort
=end

# What APPRAISE has to say for something to go down the chute
TRASH_UNDER = 10_000

# What ;stash put in the vault
STASH_LIST = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash.yaml')
# Every value APPRAISE gave, by name
VALUES = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'trash-sort.yaml')

# Crafting materials: not tools, so appraised like anything else. Matched on
# the name up to its noun, "deed" in "deed for a large pumice rock".
MATERIALS = /\b(?:ingots?|nuggets?|bars?|lumps?|fragments?|shards?|ore|lumber|logs?|limbs?|branch(?:es)?|deeds?|
               stacks?|stones?|pebbles?|rocks?|boulders?|beads?|sigil-scrolls?|leathers?|pelts?|hides?|skins?|cloth|
               yarn|thread|dyes?)$/xi
# Cloths that are tools, not materials
TOOL_CLOTHS = /\b(?:chamois|cleaning|polishing)\b/i
# Crafting supplies, kept like the tools ("flask of oil", "borax flux")
SUPPLIES = /\b(?:instructions|book|logbook|fount|flux|oil)$/i
# What ;unstash marathon gets out for ;taskmaster marathon (unstash.lic's
# MARATHON_STOCK)
MARATHON_STOCK = /\b(?:burlap cloth|rat-pelt leather|wool yarn|cotton thread)$/i
# The sorter's categories (base-sorting.yaml) for crafting gear and for
# keeping things. Its material categories aren't here: materials get appraised.
PROTECTED_CATEGORIES = /\A(?:crafting|stacker|trainer|container|box)\b/i

# Getting in and out of the vault: the same steps and messages as ;stash
ARCHES = ['go blackwood arch', 'go ironwood arch', 'go rosewood arch'].freeze
ARCH_IN = /escorts you through/
RENT_DUE = /\brent\b/i
ARCH_RESTRICTED = /access to that arch is restricted/
ARCH_BUSY = /is using that booth|blocks|someone|using|Sorry/
LEVER_PULLED = /door pops open/
VAULT_OPENED = [/^The vault opens/, /already open/i].freeze
CHAMBER = /Chamber/

# bput returns only the matched text, so these run to the end of the line.
# RUMMAGE lists the whole vault, as inventory-manager reads it: "You rummage
# through a secure vault and see a large shelf, some heavy wool cloth and a
# massive selatila shard."
RUMMAGED = /^You rummage .* and see .*/
RUMMAGED_EMPTY = /^You rummage .* but there is nothing in there/
VAULT_LIST = /^In the .* you see .*/
VAULT_EMPTY = /^There is nothing in there/
# What LOOK lists last when the vault holds more than it shows
CUT_SHORT = /\A(?:lot of )?other stuff\z/
GET_SUCCESS = [/^You get .*/, /^You pick up .*/].freeze
NOT_FOUND = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/].freeze
GET_REFUSED = [/^You need a free hand/, /^You can't/, /^Please rephrase/].freeze
APPRAISED = [/\bis a container\./, /\bworth\b.*/].freeze
APPRAISE_FAILED = [/^Appraise what/, /^You can't appraise/].freeze
KRONARS = /\bworth (?:exactly|about|around) ([\d,]+) Kronars\b/
# "You drop a steel ingot into the garbage chute.  A flap prevents it from
# falling all the way down until you leave the chamber." (2026-11-10)
CHUTE_DROPPED = /^You drop .* into the garbage chute/
PUT_SUCCESS = /^You put .*/

def hands_empty?
  DRC.right_hand.nil? && DRC.left_hand.nil?
end

# The hand display and room title can lag the game text by a moment
def settle
  10.times do
    return true if yield

    pause 0.1
  end
  false
end

def in_chamber?
  [XMLData.room_title, XMLData.room_name].any? { |title| title.to_s =~ CHAMBER }
end

# Walks to the hometown's Carousel and opens your vault, as ;stash does.
# Remembers how far it got in @vault_steps. Says why and returns false if it
# can't.
def open_vault(settings)
  @vault_steps = []
  room = get_data('town')[settings.hometown]&.dig('vault', 'id')
  unless room
    DRC.message("trash-sort: no vault listed for your hometown, #{settings.hometown}.")
    return false
  end
  unless DRCT.walk_to(room)
    DRC.message("trash-sort: couldn't walk to the Carousel (room #{room}).")
    return false
  end
  return false unless enter_booth

  unless DRC.bput('pull lever', LEVER_PULLED, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/) =~ LEVER_PULLED
    DRC.message("trash-sort: pulling the lever didn't open the door.")
    return false
  end

  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/)
  unless settle { in_chamber? }
    DRC.message("trash-sort: GO DOOR didn't reach the Carousel Chamber. Room: #{XMLData.room_title.inspect}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :chamber

  result = DRC.bput('open vault', *VAULT_OPENED, RENT_DUE, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/)
  unless VAULT_OPENED.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
    DRC.message("trash-sort: the vault didn't open: #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :open
  true
end

# Through the first arch whose booth is free, waiting a while if all are in use
def enter_booth
  6.times do
    ARCHES.each do |arch|
      result = DRC.bput(arch, ARCH_IN, RENT_DUE, ARCH_RESTRICTED, ARCH_BUSY, *NOT_FOUND)
      if result =~ ARCH_IN
        @vault_steps << :booth
        return true
      end
      if result =~ RENT_DUE
        DRC.message('trash-sort: vault rent is due. Pay it at the Carousel desk (GO DESK), then try again.')
        return false
      end
      if NOT_FOUND.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
        DRC.message("trash-sort: there's no #{arch.split[1]} arch here, so stopping.")
        return false
      end
    end
    DRC.message('trash-sort: every booth is busy. Waiting 10 seconds.')
    pause 10
  end
  DRC.message('trash-sort: gave up waiting for a free booth.')
  false
end

# Back out to the Carousel, as far as open_vault got. Only when the vault
# never opened: once it's open you stay, to check the chute.
def back_out
  steps = @vault_steps.to_a
  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/) if steps.include?(:chamber)
  DRC.bput('go arch', /door slams closed/, /.+/) if steps.include?(:booth)
end

# What's in the vault, by the names RUMMAGE gives, or LOOK IN if RUMMAGE
# doesn't answer: "You rummage through a secure vault and see a large shelf,
# some heavy wool cloth and a massive selatila shard."
def vault_contents
  result = DRC.bput('rummage vault', RUMMAGED, RUMMAGED_EMPTY, *NOT_FOUND)
  return [] if result =~ RUMMAGED_EMPTY

  if result =~ RUMMAGED
    listed = result.sub(/^You rummage .*? and see /, '')
  else
    unless @said_look
      DRC.message('trash-sort: RUMMAGE VAULT gave no list, so going by LOOK IN VAULT.')
      @said_look = true
    end
    result = DRC.bput('look in vault', VAULT_LIST, VAULT_EMPTY, *NOT_FOUND)
    return [] unless result =~ VAULT_LIST

    listed = result.sub(/^In the .*? you see /, '')
  end
  listed.sub(/\A(?:some|an|a) /, '').sub(/\.\z/, '')
        .split(/(?:,|\band) (?:some|an|a) /).map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
end

# The name up to its noun: "deed" for "deed for a large pumice rock",
# "intricate paradox sigil-scroll" for "... comprised of broad strokes"
def short_name(name, noun)
  words = name.split
  at = noun && words.index { |word| word.casecmp?(noun) }
  at ? words[0..at].join(' ') : name
end

# Every word of one of these names is in the name ("windsteel awl", "stirring
# rod" in "windsteel stirring rod")
def named?(name, names)
  words = name.downcase.split
  names.any? do |wanted|
    wanted_words = wanted.to_s.downcase.tr('.', ' ').split
    !wanted_words.empty? && (wanted_words - words).empty?
  end
end

# Why something mustn't be thrown out without even picking it up, or nil
def protected_reason(name, noun)
  short = short_name(name, noun)
  names = [name, short].uniq
  return 'for ;taskmaster marathon' if names.any? { |each| each =~ MARATHON_STOCK }
  return 'a weapon or gear' if named?(name, @gear)
  return 'a crafting tool' if named?(name, @tools) || @stashed_tools.include?(name.downcase)
  return nil if short =~ MATERIALS && name !~ TOOL_CLOTHS
  return 'a crafting supply' if names.any? { |each| each =~ SUPPLIES }

  category = @sorting.find { |_category, pattern| names.any? { |each| each =~ pattern } }&.first
  "sorted as #{category}" if category
end

# The sorter's protected categories, as [category, pattern] like sorter.lic
# builds them ("pattern" ends each entry with $)
def protected_sorting
  get_data('sorting').to_h.filter_map do |key, entries|
    category = key.to_s.sub(/_nouns|_types/, '')
    next unless category =~ PROTECTED_CATEGORIES && entries.is_a?(Array) && !entries.empty?

    [category, /(?:#{entries.join('$|')}$)/i]
  end
end

# The crafting tools named in your yaml
def crafting_tools(settings)
  %w[forging shaping enchanting outfitting alchemy].flat_map { |discipline| settings.send("#{discipline}_tools").to_a }
end

# Your weapons and gear, from the yaml: weapon_training and gear
def gear_names(settings)
  gear = settings.gear.to_a.filter_map do |piece|
    next unless piece.is_a?(Hash)

    [piece[:adjective] || piece['adjective'], piece[:name] || piece['name']].compact.join(' ')
  end
  gear + settings.weapon_training.to_h.values.map(&:to_s)
end

# What ;stash put in the vault as tools and supplies: not its materials,
# extras or weapons (weapons have no name)
def stashed_tools(list)
  list.filter_map do |entry|
    next if entry['kind'] == 'materials' || Array(entry['for']).include?('extras')

    entry['name']&.downcase
  end
end

# The ways to ask the vault for a name: the last two words, each other word
# with the noun, then the noun alone (as ;unstash does)
def addresses_for(name, noun)
  words = short_name(name, noun).split
  noun = words.last
  ([words.last(2).join(' ')] + words[0...-1].reverse.map { |word| "#{word} #{noun}" } + [noun]).uniq
end

# What GET handed over: "You get a concise contract marked with the crest of
# the Traders' Guild from inside a secure vault." gives the contract's name
def got_name(result)
  result[/^You (?:get|pick up) (?:an? |some |the |your )?(.+?) from inside\b/, 1] ||
    result[/^You (?:get|pick up) (?:an? |some |the |your )?(.+?)(?: (?:from|off) .*)?\.?\z/, 1]
end

# GET handed over this thing, though maybe by its full name ("concise
# contract" for "concise contract marked with ...", "rock pumice deed" for
# "deed for a large pumice rock")
def right_item?(got, name)
  return false unless got
  return true if got.casecmp?(name) || got.downcase.start_with?("#{name.downcase} ")

  (name.downcase.split - got.downcase.split).empty?
end

# Gets one of these out of the vault by its names. Returns the name GET gave
# with it in hand, or nil. Something else that answers to a name goes back.
def take_out(name)
  addresses_for(name, nil).each do |address|
    result = DRC.bput("get #{address} from vault", *GET_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND, *GET_REFUSED)
    next unless GET_SUCCESS.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern } && settle { !hands_empty? }

    got = got_name(result)
    return got || name if right_item?(got, name)

    put_in_vault(address.split.last)
  end
  nil
end

# Back in the vault. Stops the script if it's still in your hand.
def put_in_vault(noun)
  return if DRC.bput("put my #{noun} in vault", PUT_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND, /no room/i, /^You can't/) =~ PUT_SUCCESS && settle { hands_empty? }

  DRC.message("trash-sort: couldn't put the #{noun} back in the vault. It's still in your hand, so stopping.")
  exit
end

def into_chute?(noun)
  DRC.bput("put my #{noun} in chute", CHUTE_DROPPED, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/) =~ CHUTE_DROPPED && settle { hands_empty? }
end

# What APPRAISE says the thing in hand is worth: [Kronars or nil, what it said]
def appraise(noun)
  result = DRC.bput("appraise my #{noun}", *APPRAISED, *APPRAISE_FAILED)
  waitrt?
  return [nil, 'a container'] if result =~ /is a container/
  return [nil, result.empty? ? 'no answer' : result] unless result =~ KRONARS

  [Regexp.last_match(1).delete(',').to_i, result]
end

# Appraised at 10K or more on an earlier run, so no need to again
def kept_before?(name)
  before = @values[name]
  before.is_a?(Hash) && before['result'] == 'kept' && before['value'].is_a?(Integer) && before['value'] >= TRASH_UNDER
end

# Takes ;stash's entry for something thrown out off its list
def forget_stashed(name)
  at = @stash_list.index { |entry| entry['name'].to_s.casecmp?(name) }
  return unless at

  @stash_list.delete_at(at)
  @stash_changed = true
end

# Sorts out one thing in the vault, by the name the vault lists it under.
# Returns :thrown, :kept, :protected or :skipped.
def sort_out(name)
  reason = protected_reason(name, nil)
  if reason
    @protected[reason] << name
    return :protected
  end
  if kept_before?(name)
    @kept << "#{name} (#{with_commas(@values[name]['value'])}, appraised before)"
    return :kept
  end

  got = take_out(name)
  unless got
    @skipped << name
    return :skipped
  end

  noun = name.split.last
  # GET can hand over a longer-named thing ("thin electroweave cloth" for
  # "electroweave cloth"): that one has to be fair game too
  reason = protected_reason(got, noun)
  if reason
    put_in_vault(noun)
    @protected[reason] << got
    return :protected
  end

  value, said = appraise(noun)
  @values[got] = { 'value' => value || said, 'appraised' => Time.now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M') }
  if value && value < TRASH_UNDER && into_chute?(noun)
    @trashed << "#{got} (#{with_commas(value)})"
    @values[got]['result'] = 'thrown out'
    forget_stashed(got)
    return :thrown
  end

  put_in_vault(noun)
  @values[got]['result'] = 'kept'
  @kept << "#{got} (#{value ? with_commas(value) : said})"
  :kept
end

# Sorts out everything the vault lists. If the list ends with "a lot of other
# stuff", it's listed again while things go down the chute, since that lets
# it show more. Things with the same name are taken one at a time; once one
# isn't thrown out, the rest of that name are left, as the next GET might
# only find the same one again. Returns true if the list still ended with "a
# lot of other stuff".
def sort_out_vault
  settled = []
  loop do
    names = vault_contents
    more = names.any? { |name| name =~ CUT_SHORT }
    threw = false
    names.reject { |name| name =~ CUT_SHORT || settled.include?(name) }.tally.each do |name, count|
      count.times do
        result = sort_out(name)
        threw ||= result == :thrown
        next if result == :thrown

        settled << name
        break
      end
    end
    return more unless more && threw
  end
end

# 25000 as "25,000"
def with_commas(number)
  number.to_s.reverse.scan(/\d{1,3}/).join(',').reverse
end

def load_yaml(path, default)
  File.exist?(path) ? YAML.safe_load(File.read(path)) || default : default
end

def save_files
  FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(VALUES))
  File.write(VALUES, @values.to_yaml)
  File.write(STASH_LIST, @stash_list.to_yaml) if @stash_changed
end

unless hands_empty?
  DRC.message('trash-sort: empty your hands first.')
  exit
end
if %w[stash unstash].any? { |name| Script.running?(name) }
  DRC.message('trash-sort: ;stash or ;unstash is running. Try again once it has finished.')
  exit
end

settings = get_settings
@stash_list = load_yaml(STASH_LIST, [])
@stashed_tools = stashed_tools(@stash_list)
@tools = crafting_tools(settings)
@gear = gear_names(settings)
@sorting = protected_sorting
@values = load_yaml(VALUES, {})
@trashed = []
@kept = []
@protected = Hash.new { |hash, reason| hash[reason] = [] }
@skipped = []

unless open_vault(settings)
  back_out
  exit
end

begin
  cut_short = sort_out_vault
ensure
  save_files
end

DRC.message("trash-sort: kept, worth 10K or more or no exact figure: #{@kept.join(', ')}") unless @kept.empty?
@protected.each do |reason, names|
  listed = names.tally.map { |name, count| count > 1 ? "#{name} (#{count})" : name }
  DRC.message("trash-sort: never touched, #{reason}: #{listed.join(', ')}")
end
DRC.message("trash-sort: couldn't pick up, left in the vault: #{@skipped.uniq.join(', ')}") unless @skipped.empty?
DRC.message("trash-sort: the vault's list still ends with \"a lot of other stuff\", so some of it wasn't looked at.") if cut_short
DRC.message("trash-sort: values written to #{VALUES}")
DRC.message('trash-sort: took what went down the chute off the stash list.') if @stash_changed
if @trashed.empty?
  DRC.message('trash-sort: nothing in the vault was worth less than 10K Kronars, so nothing went down the chute.')
else
  DRC.message("trash-sort: down the chute: #{@trashed.join(', ')}")
  DRC.message("I've thrown out items under 10K kronars, check the chute for anything you still want to keep!")
  DRC.message("trash-sort: you're still in the vault chamber with the vault open. The chute empties when you leave, so CLOSE VAULT and go once you've checked it.")
end
